    "6a2fb62f-79e7-42de-acea-4e5fab243fb0": {
      "type": "columns-1",
      "blocks": {
        "12d522a9-b741-4d4c-9b79-bb469c9fa36d": {
          "type": "dropdown",
          "settings": {
            "reveal": true,
            "title": "Transfer, Rescheduling, Default, Cancellation, Termination, and Damages Fee",
            "text": "",
            "dropdown_text": "<p><strong>A.</strong> Transfer: Registration fees are non-transferable.</p><p><strong>B.</strong> Rescheduling: Vibravision® event immersions registrations may be transferred to a later event for a fee of $500. Rescheduling will not be accepted within 2 weeks of the event.</p><p><strong>C.</strong> Default: Customer’s account must be current under these Terms before the start of the Vibravision® Immersion event.</p><p><strong>D.</strong> Cancellation and refunds: Vibravision® Immersion registration fees (deposits and full pays) are non-refundable. Should our admissions directors decide for any reason to issue a refund, you are responsible for paying payment processor processing fees.</p><p><strong>E.</strong> No-Show: No refund or other credit will be provided if Customer fails to both 1) attend the Vibravision® event and 2) obtain advance written consent from Vibravision®’s admissions to reschedule to a different date</p>",
            "background_color": "#2e2767",
            "text_color": "#ffffff"
          }
        },
        "8b288a22-fe25-4939-a8bc-2bd82abe3281": {
          "type": "dropdown",
          "settings": {
            "reveal": false,
            "title": "General Provisions",
            "text": "",
            "dropdown_text": "<p><strong>A.</strong> Warranties: Customer acknowledges that Customer is not relying upon any warranties, promises, guarantees or representations made by Vibravision® or anyone acting or claiming to act on behalf of Vibravision® unless it is in writing and made a part of these Terms. All advertising material and all prior representations or agreements, if any, whether oral or written, are hereby superseded by these Terms. These Terms contains the entire understanding and agreement between Customer and Vibravision®, and no addition or modification of any of the terms herein shall be effective unless set forth in writing and signed by Customer and no Vibravision® representative has authority to modify any of these Terms.</p><p><strong>B.</strong> Terms and Conditions: By signing up and registering for this Vibravision® Event, the Customer is agreeing to be bound by these Terms, including all the Terms and Conditions herein. These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of Utah.</p><p><strong>C.</strong> Dates, times, and structure of the Vibravision® Events are subject to change. If the date is changed you will be given the option to transfer to a later event or receive a full refund.</p><p><strong>D.</strong> Vibravision® reserves the right to terminate this enrollment for any reason it deems appropriate. Tuition credits and refunds will be reviewed on a case-by-case basis.</p><p><strong>E.</strong> Assignment: This agreement may not be assigned to another individual or entity without express written approval of Vibravision®.</p><p><strong>F.</strong> Further Releases: At Vibravision® sole discretion, Vibravision® may require you to agree to additional terms and conditions to attend the Vibravision® Event. Such additional terms shall be in addition to, and shall not supersede these Terms, and these Terms shall continue in full force and effect.</p><p><strong>G.</strong> Personal Use and No Recording: You agree that by participation in or attending this Vibravision® Event, you expressly agree not to record by audio, video, photography or any other means, any portion of this Vibravision® Event, nor will you publish, post on the internet or otherwise make publicly available any recording of any portion of this Vibravision® Event. You also understand and agree that all written and/or electronic materials provided by Vibravision in connection with the Vibravision® Event are protected by the copyright laws, and you agree not to use any and all such written/electronic materials in any form after this Vibravision® Event, other than for your personal use.</p>",
            "background_color": "#2e2767",
            "text_color": "#ffffff"
          }
        },
        "88fe273d-dad8-4fcb-8e72-e298aeffea83": {
          "type": "dropdown",
          "settings": {
            "reveal": false,
            "title": "Code of Conduct and Event Security",
            "text": "",
            "dropdown_text": "<p><strong>A</strong>. Vibravision® Events maintain a strict code of conduct that all attendees must follow. Any violation of this code of conduct may result in the immediate expulsion from the event without a refund. The following is a list of rules and guidelines that attendees must abide by:</p><ul><li>Respect Others: All attendees must treat each other with respect and dignity, regardless of their background, gender, age, race, religion, or any other factor.</li><li>No Harassment or Discrimination: Harassment and discrimination of any kind, including but not limited to sexual harassment, racial discrimination, and verbal abuse, will not be tolerated. Any attendee found engaging in such behavior will be immediately expelled from the event without a refund.</li><li>No Illegal or Unsafe Activity: Attendees must not engage in any illegal activity or unsafe behavior, including but not limited to drug use, violence, theft, and destruction of property. Any attendee found engaging in such activity will be immediately expelled from the event without a refund and may be reported to the authorities.</li><li>Follow Instructions: Attendees must follow all instructions given by Vibravision® staff and organizers, including but not limited to event schedules, safety guidelines, and emergency procedures.</li><li>Respect Property: Attendees must respect the property of the event venue and other attendees. Any damage caused to property will be the responsibility of the attendee who caused it.</li><li>No Recording: Attendees are not allowed to record any portion of the Vibravision® Immersion event by audio, video, photography or any other means, nor will they publish, post on the internet or otherwise make publicly available any recording of any portion of the event.</li><li>Confidentiality: Attendees must sign a Confidentiality Agreement and Waiver of Liability prior to the start of the Immersion as a condition of attendance. Any breach of confidentiality may result in legal action.</li></ul><p>Vibravision® staff and organizers reserve the right to modify this code of conduct at any time. Attendees will be notified of any changes to the code of conduct as soon as possible.</p><p><strong>B</strong>. The Vibravision® staff and organizers have the right to remove any attendee from the event, at any time, if they exhibit behavior deemed inappropriate, disruptive, or unsafe by Vibravision®. The decision of the Vibravision® staff and organizers regarding such removals shall be final and binding.</p><p><strong>C.</strong> In order to attend a Level 2 Immersion Event, the participant must have completed a full Level 1 Immersion Event.</p><p><strong>D</strong>. In order to attend a Level 3 Immersion Event, the participant must have completed a full Level 1 Immersion Event and a full Level 2 Immersion Event. Additionally, the participant must have received an invitation from one of the master trainers to attend the Level 3 Immersion Event.</p><p><strong>E</strong>. All attendees may be subject to additional security measures, including but not limited to bag checks, metal detectors, and pat-downs, at the discretion of Vibravision® staff and organizers.</p><p><strong>F</strong>. Attendees must comply with all security measures and any other instructions or rules given by Vibravision® staff and organizers in relation to event security.</p><p><strong>G</strong>. Vibravision® staff and organizers shall not be responsible for any loss, theft, or damage to personal property or injuries sustained by attendees during the event, whether caused by the actions of other attendees or otherwise. Attendees assume all risks associated with attending the Vibravision® event.</p>",
            "background_color": "#2e2767",
            "text_color": "#ffffff"
          }
        },
        "8fef7e85-3dbd-4573-b556-4afbf969813d": {
          "type": "dropdown",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "reveal": false,
            "title": "Waiver of Responsibility",
            "text": "",
            "dropdown_text": "<p>I, the undersigned participant, acknowledge that my participation in the \"The Viking Initiation | Norway 2023\" event (hereinafter referred to as the \"Event\") hosted by Yager Transformation Group, LLC, a Delaware limited liability company (the “Company\"), involves known and unanticipated risks and hazards. These risks include, but are not limited to, physical or emotional injury, paralysis, death, and damage to myself, to property, or to third parties. I understand that such risks cannot be completely eliminated and may be caused by varying conditions such as terrain, facilities, temperature, weather, lack of hydration, physical condition of participants, equipment malfunctions, vehicular traffic, and actions of others, including but not limited to, participants, volunteers, spectators, event officials, event monitors, and/or producers of the Event.<br/></p><p>Assumption of Risks<br/><br/>I affirm that I fully understand the nature and extent of the risks involved in the Event. By signing this form, I voluntarily agree to accept and assume all risks, both known and unknown, inherent or otherwise, associated with my participation in the Event. I assume full and complete responsibility for any injuries, damages, losses, liabilities, costs, or expenses that I incur as a result of participating in the Event.</p><p>Health Declaration<br/><br/>I hereby certify that I have either:<br/><br/>(a) undergone a comprehensive physical examination and have been given medical clearance by a qualified healthcare provider to participate in the Event; or<br/>(b) chosen to participate in the Event without seeking medical advice and clearance.<br/></p><p>I acknowledge and accept full responsibility for this decision and its potential implications. I hereby release, discharge, and covenant not to sue the Company and all other parties affiliated with the Event, including but not limited to, its parent companies, affiliates, subsidiaries, event organizers, sponsors, event directors, officials, contractors, advertisers, volunteers, staff, agents, representatives, and each of their respective insurance carriers, underwriters, subrogated agents, successors, and assigns (collectively, \"Releasees\"), from any and all liability, claims, demands, legal actions, and causes of action whatsoever, arising out of or related to any loss, damage, or injury, including death, that may be sustained by me or to any property belonging to me, related to such a decision, whether arising from the negligence of the Releasees or otherwise.<br/></p><p>Waiver of Liability and Indemnification<br/><br/>In consideration for allowing my participation in the Event, I voluntarily agree to the following:<br/><br/>(A) To waive, relinquish, discharge, release, and covenant not to sue the Company and Releasees from any and all claims arising from or related to any direct, indirect, incidental or consequential damages, injuries, losses, or death that I may suffer as a result of my participation in the Event.<br/><br/>(B) To indemnify and hold harmless the Company and Releasees against any and all legal claims, actions, suits, procedures, costs, expenses, damages, and liabilities,<br/>including attorney's fees, arising out of or related to my actions or conduct during the Event.<br/><br/>(C) To consent to receive medical treatment, including but not limited to first aid or emergency medical services, as may be deemed advisable in the event of injury, accident, and/or illness during the Event. I acknowledge and understand that I will be responsible for any and all medical and related bills that may be incurred as a result of any medical treatment for me.<br/><br/>Governing Law and Broad Interpretation<br/><br/>This Accident Waiver and Release of Liability Form shall be construed broadly to provide a release and waiver to the maximum extent permissible under the applicable law of Delaware. I certify that I have read, understood, and voluntarily agree to the terms stipulated in this document.<br/></p>",
            "background_color": "#2e2767",
            "text_color": "#ffffff"
          }
        },
        "fada70bb-9ebc-48cd-87d2-ba2bb418ab07": {
          "type": "dropdown",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "reveal": false,
            "title": "Changes",
            "text": "",
            "dropdown_text": "<p>This Itinerary is subject to changes. The content will remain the same, barring any unanticipated complications, and will include many delightful “extras” and surprises.</p>",
            "background_color": "#2e2767",
            "text_color": "#ffffff"
          }
        },
        "36d254e6-c118-4eb9-868e-c7838412525e": {
          "type": "dropdown",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "reveal": false,
            "title": "Insurance",
            "text": "",
            "dropdown_text": "<p>We highly recommend that all participants obtain travel insurance. Travel Insured International offers insurance for trip cost, trip cancellation & interruption, and pays for loss due to unforeseen circumstance, death, injury, or illness to you or a member of your family. It also includes coverage for missed connections due to weather, pays for lost deposits due to the financial default of the airline, the tour operator, or cruise line. It pays for baggage delays, travel delays, medical expenses and emergency assistance.</p>",
            "background_color": "#2e2767",
            "text_color": "#ffffff"
          }
        }
      },
